#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:2
msgid "Deploy for Out-of-Band (OOB) Communications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:4
msgid ""
"When a critical incident disrupts an organization’s primary "
"infrastructure—due to a cyberattack, cloud outage, or internal failure—a "
"secure, independent communication channel becomes essential. Mattermost "
"can serve as that channel by operating in an Out-of-Band (OOB) "
"environment: isolated, pre-provisioned, and ready to support incident "
"response and business continuity teams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:6
msgid ""
"This document outlines architectural guidance for deploying Mattermost in"
" an OOB scenario across `generic <#generic-oob-architecture>`__, `AWS "
"<#aws-based-oob-deployment>`__, and `Azure <#azure-based-oob-"
"deployment>`__ environments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:9
msgid "Generic OOB architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:11
msgid ""
"This platform-agnostic design establishes a fallback communication "
"system, decoupled from primary networks and identity providers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:13
msgid "Generic OOB Architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:18
msgid "Architecture components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:20
msgid ""
"**Users (Cybersecurity, IR Teams)**: Pre-authorized personnel trained to "
"access and use the OOB platform during emergencies. Credentials and "
"access methods should be provisioned in advance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:21
msgid ""
"**Secure Access Layer**: A firewall or access gateway protecting entry "
"into the OOB environment. May include network policies, IP allowlists, or"
" WAFs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:22
msgid ""
"**Secondary IdP / Emergency Auth**: A dedicated identity provider not "
"dependent on the organization’s primary SSO or IdP (e.g., a minimal Azure"
" AD tenant, Okta org, or locally stored credentials with MFA)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:23
msgid ""
"**VPN / Bastion Host**: A hardened jumpbox or independent VPN granting "
"access to internal OOB components and Kubernetes control plane."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:24
msgid ""
"**Failover DNS Manager**: Services like Cloudflare Load Balancer, Azure "
"Traffic Manager, or Route 53 to monitor primary system health and reroute"
" DNS to the OOB ingress."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:25
msgid ""
"**Ingress Controller**: e.g., ingress-nginx to handle HTTP(S) routing "
"within the cluster, directing traffic to Mattermost Web, API, and "
"WebSocket endpoints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:26
msgid ""
"**Mattermost Operator & App**: Automates lifecycle of Mattermost "
"instances in Kubernetes; ensures updates, scaling, and configuration "
"consistency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:27
msgid ""
"**PostgreSQL Database**: Persistent storage for channels, messages, "
"users, and configurations; can be self-hosted or managed externally with "
"hardened access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:28
msgid "**Backups**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:30
msgid ""
"**Velero**: Backs up Kubernetes resources to external object store (S3, "
"Blob)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:31
msgid ""
"**pg_dump / Cloud-native backup**: Regular logical exports or managed "
"backups."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:32
msgid ""
"**Object Storage**: Durable, versioned storage (e.g., S3, Azure Blob) for"
" snapshots and dumps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:35
msgid "AWS-based OOB deployment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:37
msgid ""
"Deploying Mattermost in AWS leverages managed services and strong "
"isolation capabilities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:39
msgid "AWS OOB Deployment diagram"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:44
msgid "AWS components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:46
msgid ""
"**Amazon EKS**: Managed Kubernetes for Mattermost Operator and "
"application, with HA and auto-scaling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:47
msgid ""
"**Route 53**: DNS service for health-checked failover to the OOB "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:48
msgid ""
"**Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL**: High-performance managed PostgreSQL with "
"automated failovers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:49
msgid ""
"**Amazon S3**: Object storage for Velero snapshots, configurations, and "
"database backups (with versioning and cross-region replication)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:50
msgid ""
"**IAM Roles**: Scoped roles for EKS nodes and Velero using IRSA, "
"enforcing least-privilege."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:54
msgid "Use separate AWS accounts or VPCs for full isolation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:55
msgid "Configure Route 53 health checks against public or synthetic endpoints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:56
msgid "Encrypt secrets and enforce least-privilege IAM policies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:59
msgid "Azure-Based OOB deployment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:61
msgid ""
"For Azure customers, AKS and related services provide a robust OOB "
"platform for Mattermost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:63
msgid "Azure OOB Deployment diagram"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:68
msgid "Azure components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:70
msgid ""
"**Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)**: Runs Mattermost workloads with native"
" autoscaling and Azure AD integration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:71
msgid ""
"**Azure DNS + Traffic Manager**: Global traffic routing and DNS failover "
"based on endpoint health."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:72
msgid ""
"**Azure Database for PostgreSQL**: Managed DB service with automated "
"backups and patching."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:73
msgid ""
"**Azure Blob Storage**: Destination for Velero snapshots and DB dumps; "
"supports lifecycle policies and secure access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:74
msgid ""
"**Azure AD (Secondary Tenant)**: Acts as the IdP for OOB; deployed in a "
"separate directory with scoped permissions and MFA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:78
msgid "Deploy in a dedicated subscription for security and billing separation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:79
msgid "Use Azure Monitor for health checks and Traffic Manager probes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:80
msgid ""
"Harden AKS node pools and isolate workloads with namespaces and network "
"policies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:83
msgid "Operational guidelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:89
msgid "**Domain**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:90
msgid "**Recommendation**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:91
msgid "Access Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:92
msgid ""
"Isolate authentication from primary infrastructure. Use MFA, secure "
"vaults, and emergency tokens. Preload user accounts in the secondary IdP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:93
msgid "DNS Failover"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:94
msgid ""
"Employ TTL-aware health checks via Route 53 or Traffic Manager. Monitor "
"critical HTTP(S) or TCP endpoints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:95
msgid "Backup Strategy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:96
msgid ""
"Schedule frequent Velero and database backups. Store in versioned, "
"encrypted object storage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:97
msgid "Disaster Recovery Drills"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:98
msgid ""
"Conduct quarterly failover exercises: DNS switching, Mattermost access, "
"and data restores."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:99
msgid "Security"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:100
msgid ""
"Treat OOB as Tier 0. Use hardened OS images, audit logging, strict RBAC, "
"and centralized monitoring. Rotate secrets regularly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/reference-architecture/deployment-scenarios/deploy-oob.rst:102
msgid ""
"Mattermost can be an effective OOB communication platform when deployed "
"with isolation, automation, and operational readiness. Whether on AWS, "
"Azure, or a generic environment, prioritize independence, simplicity, and"
" resilience. Pair these designs with standard IR playbooks and routine "
"failover testing to build a confident, secure response capability."
msgstr ""

